---
// Want a photo? Put it in src/assets/, import it, and add
// <Image src={portrait} alt="…" class="portrait" /> from 'astro:assets' before .text.
---

<section id="about" class="section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="text">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 — About</span>
      <h2 id="about-title" class="visually-hidden">About me</h2>
      <p class="statement">
        The best data products answer the question you were about to ask.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        I came to engineering from finance and insurance, so I gravitate to products about money
        and metrics: reporting at Mailchimp, internal tools for 30,000 people at Nationwide, and on
        my own time, <a href="/work/meridian/">Meridian</a> and <a href="/work/caldera/">Caldera</a>.
        Next: a frontend role on an analytics, data or fintech team.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .split {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(20px, 5.5vw, 80px);
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 360px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .text {
    max-width: 760px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .statement {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2.125rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .muted {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .split {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .portrait {
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    }
  }
</style>
